/*
 * disclose-boundary.compact — disclose() is not a publish.
 *
 * Official reads (not invented APIs):
 *   https://docs.midnight.network/guides/security-best-practices
 *   "Wrapping a value in disclose() does not publish it. disclose() clears
 *    the compiler's private-data check so the value may cross a public
 *    boundary; the value becomes visible only when it crosses one, through
 *    a ledger write, a return from an exported circuit, or a
 *    contract-to-contract call."
 *   https://docs.midnight.network/compact/reference/explicit-disclosure
 *
 * Upstream: midnightntwrk/midnight-docs#1245
 * The cross-chain guide says a disclose() call publishes. That contradicts
 * the security page the same guide links. This file does not edit that guide.
 *
 * Language pin: Compact ~0.31.1 / language ~0.23.
 * LOCAL-TRUE. Source only. Not compiled here. Not deployed.
 * This file does not fix the public indexer or node.
 *
 * Built by @kshot9000 https://x.com/kshot9000
